**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** What a kit references in the library, as data (001 §E 'Library closure snapshot: every library version the kit references is copied into library/ when first referenced, built-ins included'; the S4.2 brief: a kit first references a library version by binding a sample, material or preset). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs`, directly before `LibraryEntryContent` (step 25), each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S4.2. `LibraryVersionRef = { entryId : LibraryEntryId; version : VersionNumber }` is one version of one library entry, with `member this.describe : string` = `<GUID> v<n>`. `EntryReference` = `EntryVersionReference of LibraryVersionRef` (a version named exactly, as a sample or a material is bound) | `EntryLatestReference of LibraryEntryId` (an entry named by its id alone, as a preset is bound and a material names its category), with `member this.entryId : LibraryEntryId` and `member this.describe : string` (`<GUID> v<n>` or `<GUID> (latest)`). `LibraryEntryContent` gains `member this.references : EntryReference list`. A material answers its `categoryOpt` as one `EntryLatestReference`. A sample answers its `structure.referencedMaterialVersions` (step 61), in that set's order, each as the `EntryVersionReference` of its material's `toLibraryEntryId` (step 24) and version. Every other kind answers nothing. `referencedEntryIds` (step 93) becomes the set of the `entryId`s of `references`, so the references are walked in one place and its answers are unchanged. `type LibraryEntryEnvelope with member this.libraryVersionRef : LibraryVersionRef` is the content's id and version. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Lifecycle.fs` opens `LibraryEntryFiles`. `VersionRef` (`Lifecycle.fs:VersionRef`) gains `member this.entryReference : EntryReference`, the `EntryVersionReference` of the material's or the sample's id and version. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs`: `ElementBinding` (`Experiments.fs:ElementBinding`) gains `member this.entryReferenceOpt : EntryReference option`. `BoundByVersion v` is `Some v.entryReference`, `BoundByEntryId id` is `id.tryToLibraryEntryId` (step 24) as an `EntryLatestReference`, and `Unbound` is `None`. `Experiment` gains `member this.libraryReferences : EntryReference list`, its setup's bindings in setup order, each once: what a kit snapshots when it records the experiment. Each doc is one to three lines. No conversion goes the other way (ELEV006), and no other member is added. Tests. `LibraryEntryFilesTests` gains `an entry's references name a material's category at its latest and a sample's material versions`: Silicon's content (`BuiltinCatalogue.catalogueData ()`) answers exactly one `EntryLatestReference` of its `categoryOpt`'s category. `SampleIds.multilayerQwId`'s content answers the `EntryVersionReference`s of `MaterialIds.glass152` and `MaterialIds.vacuumMaterial` at version 1. A source's content answers `[]`. `an entry's references are its category and its materials` (step 93) passes unchanged. `ExperimentProxyTests` gains `an experiment references the library versions its setup binds, each once`: an experiment whose setup binds `SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId` at version 1, `PresetIds.source600` twice and one unbound element answers exactly the `EntryVersionReference` of that sample at version 1 and the `EntryLatestReference` of the source's GUID.

**Acceptance.** After the references land, `LibraryEntryContent.references` MUST name a material's category and a sample's material versions, `referencedEntryIds` MUST be their ids, and `Experiment.libraryReferences` MUST answer the setup's bindings once each; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an entry's references name a material's category at its latest and a sample's material versions` and `an experiment references the library versions its setup binds, each once`, the count rising by 2, with `an entry's references are its category and its materials` passing as written; and build, elevation and the eleven s16 invariants MUST pass.
